# xFusionCorp Industries — ML Training Docker Environment

## Project Overview

This task involved completing the Dockerfile for the fraud-detection training environment. The objective was to create a consistent Python environment, install all required dependencies, copy the existing training script into the image, and configure the default command to execute the training process.

The existing `train.py` file was preserved without modification. Only the Dockerfile was authored.

## Objectives

- Use `python:3.11-slim` as the base image.
- Set `/app` as the working directory.
- Install all Python packages required by the training script.
- Copy `train.py` into the Docker image.
- Configure the container to run the training script by default.
- Build and verify the `ml-trainer:v1` Docker image.
- Confirm that all required Python imports resolve successfully.

## Dockerfile Implementation

```dockerfile
FROM python:3.11-slim

WORKDIR /app

RUN pip install --no-cache-dir scikit-learn pandas numpy joblib

COPY train.py .

CMD ["python3", "train.py"]
```

### Dockerfile Explanation

| Instruction | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `FROM python:3.11-slim` | Uses the Python 3.11 slim base image. |
| `WORKDIR /app` | Sets the working directory inside the container. |
| `RUN pip install --no-cache-dir scikit-learn pandas numpy joblib` | Installs the required Python dependencies. |
| `COPY train.py .` | Copies the existing training script into `/app`. |
| `CMD ["python3", "train.py"]` | Runs the training script when the container starts without an overriding command. |

